<SiteLayout title={"HR & Payroll — Blue Line Capital Group"} description={"Giving people, teams and operations a dependable foundation."} lang="en">
<section class="sector-hero"><div class="sector-hero-bg"><img alt="People operations" class="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" loading="eager" src="/assets/img/people-operations.webp"/></div><div class="sector-hero-scrim"></div><div class="shell sector-hero-in"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a><span> / </span><a href="/en/businesses/">Businesses</a><span> / </span><strong>HR &amp; Payroll</strong></div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="hairline"></span>08 / People operations</div><h1>The enterprise is its people.</h1><p>A strong group needs human systems that are accurate, considerate and consistent.</p><a class="down-link" href="#overview">Discover more &darr;</a></div></section><section class="section shell two-col-editorial" id="overview"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="hairline"></span>01 / Areas of activity</div><h2>HR &amp; Payroll</h2></div><div><p class="large-copy">Giving people, teams and operations a dependable foundation.</p><p>People operations span the employee lifecycle: records, attendance, leave administration, salary processing support, expense workflows and workforce reporting. As a Group function, HR &amp; Payroll helps different business units work with a more consistent information foundation while keeping employment decisions at the right level.</p><a class="btn btn-accent" href="/en/contact/"><span>Contact the Group</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearrow;</span></a></div></section><section class="sector-capabilities"><div class="shell capabilities-layout"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="hairline"></span>02 / Where we focus</div><h2>Where we focus</h2><p>A strong group needs human systems that are accurate, considerate and consistent.</p></div><ul><li><span>01</span><strong>Employee records and lifecycle information</strong><span aria-hidden="true">&nearrow;</span></li><li><span>02</span><strong>Attendance, leave and approvals</strong><span aria-hidden="true">&nearrow;</span></li><li><span>03</span><strong>Payroll workflow and statutory-reporting support</strong><span aria-hidden="true">&nearrow;</span></li><li><span>04</span><strong>Workforce and team visibility</strong><span aria-hidden="true">&nearrow;</span></li></ul></div></section><section class="section shell"><div class="process-head"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="hairline"></span>03 / How we think about delivery</div><h2>How we think about delivery</h2></div><div class="process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Maintain accurate employee information</h3><p>A strong group needs human systems that are accurate, considerate and consistent.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Coordinate clear approvals and workflows</h3><p>People operations span the employee lifecycle: records, attendance, leave administration, salary processing support, expense workflows and workforce reporting. As a Group function, HR &amp; Payroll helps different business units work with a more consistent information foundation while keeping employment decisions at the right level.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Support reliable reporting and people decisions</h3><p>Giving people, teams and operations a dependable foundation.</p></article></div><div class="faq-block"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="hairline"></span>04 / A few practical answers</div><h2>A few practical answers</h2><details><summary>Are job vacancies managed here?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Current confirmed openings would appear on the Careers page. This site does not advertise unverified vacancies.</p></details><details><summary>Can employees access payslips on this website?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. This public presentation site is not an authenticated HR portal.</p></details></div></section><section class="related-section section"><div class="shell"><div class="split-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="hairline"></span>05 / Explore another area</div><h2>Explore another area</h2></div><a class="btn btn-ou